exp="The kidney's <b>juxtaglomerular (JG) cells</b>, which make renin, carry <b>β1 receptors</b>. Sympathetic or β1-agonist stimulation raises renin release, along with heart rate and contractility. That is also why <b>beta-blockers lower renin</b> and part of why they lower blood pressure. The other two renin triggers are low afferent arteriolar pressure and low sodium chloride delivery to the macula densa.<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> β1 receptors on renal juxtaglomerular cells stimulate renin release; β1 agonists raise renin and beta-blockers lower it.",
